35 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
faded wooden tablet~
The _-ll of the *&ea& city o- Oli*-z&i*-t&*

   The darkness spreads, even now.  So many of our kind have grown sick.
As per tradition, they have wandered far off into the bog to lead their
final moments.  But so many are sick, so many are afflicted they are starting
to die in the city.

   Our shamans have no cure for the illness, it must be magical in nature
as the spirits are not capable of stopping it.  We have asked the wolfen
tribes for help, but they ignore us.  The minotaurs are too young to
help us.  We are alone.

   Those that are not sick are preparing to leave the city, but we do not want
to infect the others.  Perhaps it is the fate of the spirits that we die.
~
#2911
oddly coated scroll~
an oddly coated scroll~
This scroll is somehow protected from the water.~
~
35 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
oddly coated scroll~
Our city must be reinforced if we hope to keep the swamp mud from crushing
the structures.  I believe our new material, the combination of melted flax
and magic will be enough to seal the wood from the damaging affects of
the water.  It is much easier to harvest the wood from the jungles
than to spend the time it takes to shape the rock.

 We have thought about teaching the scattered wolfen tribes the secret
of this new material, but our Matron states that they must develop on their
own.  They are in possession of a thread, made from some obscure
animal, that is much stronger than we possess.  I think the trade is worth it
but it is not my place to make that choice.  I will speak with the Matron
again.


~
#2912
preserved clay tablet~
a preserved clay tablet~
This clay tablet has managed to survive the water well.~
~
35 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
clay tablet preserved~
Our scouts have reported something strange.  It appears that a fleet of odd
creatures have landed in the far east, near wolfen lands.  They are tall and
lithe, quite similar to us actually.  Yet, they are not derived reptilian, nor
 are they quite mammals.  They are not covered in fur, except for the thin
patches on their head.  They seem quite sophisticated, despite not having
scales.  It makes us nervous though, to see this new breed of species emerge.
It is clear that they are not native to our land, so then it must be true that
other lands exist across the ocean.  This is not an unheard of theory, but one
we have not managed to prove one way or the other, until now. It should be
interesting to see how they interact with the wolfen, who are quite
aggressive, not unlike the creatures that prowl the swamps.  If need be, we
will step in and stop any undue war.  The wolfen tribes keep themselves well
in check through their constant wars with each other, but these creatures
might upset that delicate balance. We have no physical or spiritual proof that
these creatures are capable of great magical power, but some of our scouts
have seen them battling some of the beasts in the land.  The reports are odd
and unbelievable. They claim these creatures can call upon great powers to
heal and shield themselves, even alter the world around them.  I think our
scouts were mistaken, being taken back by seeing an entirely new race in our
lands.  We will watch them as best we can.
~
#3000
decayed wooden tablet~
a decayed wooden tablet~
This tablet is only partially legible.~
~
35 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
decayed wooden tablet~
*(&(@*yu #*(#)@ ---&&*((


  The **&$-- caused this.  I am sure.  I have pr--&*@(@&#



     It is near over now.  Our eggs will not hatch, the life inside has
    long since died.  Our warriors cannot fight what is made of air.
    The Matron has not left her throne in months.  Our people
    are dying.  I fear that I may be the last breathing resident of this
    great city.  A few parties have left these lands, they used the ships
    of those blasted creatures to find safer places.  Some of us are
    immune to the disease, but I am not.  I feel it in my blood.
    My scales have already started to rot.  I will be like the others,
    stalking the halls of the city in a zombie like state.  Soon I will
    be nothing more than a shell.  It is against the will of the spirits
    and the great serpents of fire, air, water, and death for me
   to do so.  So falls are city.  So falls our kind.
~
